+"""Native voice seam: profile-shaped ElevenLabs/STT integration controls (source coverage, NOT runtime or current-profile proof).
+
+What runs for real: ``synthesize_native_once`` / ``transcribe_native_once``, the stock config and ``.env`` secret-scope paths
+(``HERMES_HOME`` is the single served profile of the call, the declared contract), the stock STT auto-detect, the REAL installed
+``elevenlabs`` SDK and the real ``requests``/``httpx`` clients. Only the network bytes are synthetic (``native_voice_support`` and
+the existing ``Wire``/``RequestsWire`` seams). The registered cases run the core call under a REAL ``GatewayRunner`` /
+``SessionAuthority`` / Gadget adapter (``relay_native_support.home_rig``) whose ``authority.authorize`` is the consumer's
+``authorize`` callback. They are NOT a V2 bridge and NOT a runner voice-message dispatch: no such path exists yet.
+
+What this file does NOT prove, and cannot: the sentinels below are explicit synthetic values. A passing run says nothing about
+the real M5/GPU/Windows profiles, their credentials, their installed SDK versions/extras, their initialized plugin registry
+(a source-registered hook here is not the live registry), the process-global OpenTelemetry tracer provider (M1 stays OPEN
+until a controller inspects the ACTUAL initialized state), local-STT caches, the launcher/codecs of any host, or any provider
+header/quality. Those are UNKNOWN here and remain controller-owned gates.
+"""
+import asyncio
+import json
+import logging
+import os
+import shutil
+import threading
+from dataclasses import replace
+from pathlib import Path
+
+import pytest
+
+from gateway.session_contract import Principal
+from gateway.session_native_voice import synthesize_native_once, transcribe_native_once
+from hermes_state_runtime import RuntimeStoreError
