+# qualified network-deny launcher + ``run_native_argv`` as the accepted managed normalizer above: exact remaining deadline, Stop and
+# authorization at spawn, stdin DEVNULL, local-file protocols, capped streams and a size-watched output file. Optional steps
+# (probe, trim) are skipped, with NO recorded refusal, when the runner cannot be used (:func:`_native_prep_ready`), so the unchanged
+# full recording is still uploaded exactly as stock does when its tools are missing. Stop, deadline, lost authority and output
+# bounds are real refusals and always propagate. Outside a native call none of this runs.
+NATIVE_PREP_MAX_BYTES = NORMALIZED_WAV_MAX_BYTES  # one bound for every preparation output file (CAF wav, trim m4a, compaction m4a)
+_NATIVE_PROBE_INPUT = ("-v", "error", "-protocol_whitelist", "file", "-show_entries", "format=duration", "-of",
